\ At this point, we have a core set of system words and are in interpreter
\ mode. However, we don't yet have the ability to define new words. We'll
\ manually construct a new word, ":Def", which will allow us to define new
\ words.

'sysalloc @ @ 4 AlignTo 'sysalloc @ ! \ Align the heap pointer.
Tok :Def                              \ Tokenize the word: ":Def".
Dup 1 + Swap @bu ,bs                  \ Copy the token to the heap.
'sysalloc @ @ 4 AlignTo 'sysalloc @ ! \ Align the heap again.
$0000 ,h                              \ Write 0 for the code length.
$00 ,b                                \ No flags. (visible, non-immediate)
'systok @ @bu ,b                      \ Copy the token length.
'sysalloc @ @ 'sysdict @ , 'sysdict ! \ Link the new word in the dictionary.

\ Now we've manually defined the header of ":Def" in the dictionary, we'll
\ define the code of the word to effectively do the same thing we just did
\ above.

\ The main notable change is the use of ",Defer" to defer the execution of
\ "compilation words" (i.e. words that write to the heap and start with ",")
\ This is necessary as compilation words are "immediate" words: Words that are
\ executed as soon as they are encountered during compilation. ",Defer", being
\ a compilation word itself, writes the code to execute the next word
\ regardless of whether it is immediate or not.

] \ Exit interpreter mode.

\ All non-immediate words from here on will be
\ compiled into the body of ":Def".

    'sysalloc @ @ 4 AlignTo 'sysalloc @ !
    Tok
    Dup 1 + Swap @bu ,Defer ,bs
    'sysalloc @ @ 4 AlignTo 'sysalloc @ !
    $0000 ,Defer ,h
    $00 ,Defer ,b
    'systok @ @bu ,Defer ,b
    'sysalloc @ @ 'sysdict @ ,Defer , 'sysdict !
    ,Exit

[ \ Re-Enter interpreter mode.

\ Now, ":Def" will be able to take the next token and define a new word.
\ We can now use ":Def" to define some helper words for manipulating the flags
\ byte of a word's header.

:Def :@Flags
]
    'sysdict @ @ \ Get the address of the last defined word.
    2 - @bu      \ Read the flags byte.
    ,Exit
[

:Def :!Flags
]
    'sysdict @ @ \ Get the address of the last defined word.
    2 - !b       \ Write the flags byte.
    ,Exit
[

\ Mark the most recently defined word as hidden.
\ Hidden words will be skipped when searching the word list.
:Def :Hidden
]
    :@Flags $01 Or% :!Flags
    ,Exit
[

\ Mark the most recently defined word as visible (not hidden).
:Def :Visible
]
    :@Flags $FE And% :!Flags
    ,Exit
[

\ Mark the most recently defined word as immediate.
:Def :Immediate
]
    :@Flags $02 Or% :!Flags
    ,Exit
[

\ Define a new hidden word and enter compilation mode.
:Def :Fn
]
    :Def :Hidden
    ,Defer ]
    ,Exit
[

\ Mark the most recently defined word as visible, compile an ",Exit" to end
\ the function, and return to interpreter mode.
:Def ; :Immediate
]
    :Visible
    ,Defer ,Exit
    ,Defer [
    ,Exit
[

:Fn test 2 2 + ;

$4B4B $000B8000 !h
$4B4B $000B8002 !h

